# Another generator's declaration of the same override — the shape an app hits
# when a tool that reads the SOURCE (rbs_infer) emits the `def accepted?` this
# app writes, alongside the one rbs_rails derives from `enum :status`.
#
# It is only a legal override, rather than a second definition of the same
# method, because the generated predicates live in an included module. Written
# flat into the class body they collided here as
# `RBS::DuplicatedMethodDefinition`.
class User
  def accepted?: () -> bool
end
